--!strict
-- Whether normal weapon fire should be suppressed right now.
--
-- Exists because two independent input controllers can end up bound to the
-- same physical trigger: CombatController binds MouseButton1/ButtonR2 to fire
-- the equipped weapon, and TurretCCTVController binds the same inputs to fire
-- a manually-controlled turret. A higher ContextActionService priority alone
-- doesn't solve this — a mobile player's on-screen Fire button generated by
-- CombatController is its own synthetic input, delivered straight to
-- CombatController's action regardless of what else has Sunk the raw input —
-- so without this flag, taking manual control of a turret would also
-- discharge the player's own weapon every time they fired the gun.

local CombatInputLock = {
	locked = false,
}

return CombatInputLock
